    "stem": {
      "zh": "该公司为公司内的所有开发人员设置了亚马逊 Q 开发者专业版许可证。公司维护着一份开发人员在开发应用程序时必须使用的已批准资源清单。这些已批准的资源包括内部库、专有算法技术以及具有批准样式的示例代码。一个新的开发团队正在使用亚马逊 Q 开发者工具来开发一个新的基于 Java 的应用程序。公司必须确保新的开发团队使用公司批准的资源。公司不想对项目进行层级修改。哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？",
      "en": "A company has set up Amazon Q Developer Pro licenses for all developers at the company. The company maintains a list of approved resources that developers must use when developing applications. The approved resources include internal libraries, proprietary algorithmic techniques, and sample code with approved styling. A new team of developers is using Amazon Q Developer to develop a new Java-based application. The company must ensure that the new developer team uses the company’s approved resources. The company does not want to make project-level modifications. Which solution will meet these requirements?"
    },
    "options": {
      "zh": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "创建一个包含所有已批准的内部库、算法和代码示例的 Git 代码库。在本地将此 Git 代码库作为工作区的一部分包含在应用程序项目中。确保开发人员使用工作区上下文从 Git 代码库中获取建议。"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "在项目根目录下创建一个名为 amazonq/rules 的文件夹。将已获批准的内部库、算法和代码示例添加到该文件夹中。"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "在应用程序项目中创建一个名为“rules”的文件夹。将指南和代码存储在该文件夹中，以便 Amazon Q Developer 引用以获取代码建议。"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "创建一个包含已批准数据源的 Amazon Q 开发者定制版。确保开发人员使用该定制版来开发应用程序。"
        }
      ],
      "en": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "Create a Git repository that contains all of the approved internal libraries, algorithms, and code samples. Include this Git repository in the application project locally as part of the workspace. Ensure that the developers use the workspace context to retrieve suggestions from the Git repository."
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "In the project root folder, create a folder named amazonq/rules. Add the approved internal libraries, algorithms, and code samples to the folder."
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "Create a folder in the application project named rules. Store the guidelines and code in the folder for Amazon Q Developer to reference for code suggestions."
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "Create an Amazon Q Developer customization that includes the approved data sources. Ensure that the developers use the customization to develop the application."
        }
      ]
    },
    "explanation": {
      "zh": "选项 D 是正确答案，因为亚马逊 Q 开发者自定义功能旨在整合组织认可的知识和编码指南，无需针对每个项目进行更改。自定义功能可以引导亚马逊 Q 开发者指向经过筛选的内部资源，例如已获批准的库、编码规范等。标准、架构模式和专有技术。这使得助手的建议能够始终与公司政策以及各团队和代码库中的首选实现方式保持一致。关键要求是公司不想对项目层面进行修改。选项 A、B 和 C 都需要在项目工作区中添加文件或代码库，这直接违反了这一限制。它们还依赖于开发人员的行为来“使用工作区上下文”，这更难强制执行，并可能导致对标准的不一致遵循。通过定制，组织可以集中管理和更新已批准的资源。这减少了运营开销，因为对库、模式或指南的更新会自动传播给使用该定制的开发人员，而无需对每个项目进行更改。这对于新团队来说尤其有价值，因为一致地执行已批准的实践对于降低合规风险、安全问题和代码风格不一致至关重要。此外，定制功能支持治理，使公司能够标准化亚马逊 Q 开发者（Amazon Q Developer）的响应方式，确保其建议反映的是经过批准的内部内容，而非通用的公共模式。因此，选项 D 最能满足对已批准资源进行集中管理的要求，且后续管理最少，无需在项目层面进行修改。",
      "en": "Option D is the correct solution because Amazon Q Developer customizations are designed to incorporate organization-approved knowledge and coding guidance without requiring per-project changes. A customization can point Amazon Q Developer to curated internal sources such as approved libraries, coding standards, architectural patterns, and proprietary techniques. This allows the assistant’s suggestions to align with company policies and preferred implementations consistently across teams and repositories. The key requirement is that the company does not want to make project-level modifications. Options A, B, and C all require adding files or repositories into the project workspace, which directly violates this constraint. They also rely on developer behavior to “use workspace context,” which is harder to enforce and can lead to inconsistent adherence to standards. With a customization, the organization centrally manages and updates approved resources. This reduces operational overhead because updates to libraries, patterns, or guidelines propagate automatically to developers using the customization, without requiring changes to each project. This is especially valuable for a new team, where consistent enforcement of approved practices is important to reduce compliance risk, security issues, and inconsistent code style. Additionally, customizations support governance by allowing the company to standardize how Amazon Q Developer responds, ensuring that suggestions reflect approved internal content rather than generic public patterns. Therefore, Option D best satisfies the requirement for centralized enforcement of approved resources with minimal ongoing management and no project-level modifications."
    },
