    "explanation": {
      "zh": "选项 B 是正确的，因为它使用了亚马逊 Bedrock 中的托管评估功能，该功能专门用于使用一致的提示集比较基础模型，并在无需大量自定义工具的情况下生成结构化的结果。在 Bedrock 评估工作流中，您提供一个输入提示数据集，通常采用 JSON Lines 格式，这样每行代表一条评估记录。将 JSONL 文件存储在亚马逊 S3 中，可让 Bedrock 大规模读取数据集，并将标准化的评估输出写回 S3，以便进行下游分析、共享和保留。关键要求是对多个模型的质量和安全性进行全面评估。Bedrock 评估任务可以使用评判模型根据既定标准对生成的输出进行评分。这种方法支持可重复的、具有可比性的评估，因为相同的评判模型和评分标准可以应用于每个候选基础模型。候选模型被配置为生成器，这意味着每次评估任务运行时，都会使用一个选定的基础模型为相同的提示集生成答案，然后由评判模型对这些答案进行评估。这符合生成评估报告以帮助数据科学家选择最佳基础模型的要求。选项 A 不使用 Bedrock 评估任务，知识库加上检索与生成是一种 RAG 模式，而非评估框架。它会生成响应，但无法提供适合模型选择的标准化评分和报告。选项 C 不正确，因为 Bedrock 评估输出会交付到 S3，而非直接交付到商业智能（BI）目的地，并且选择候选的 FM 作为评估者与使用稳定评判模型的预期模式相冲突。选项 D 在要求是基于提示的模型评估而非评估检索质量的情况下，错误地使用了知识库和检索评估类型。",
      "en": "Option B is correct because it uses the managed evaluation capability in Amazon Bedrock that is intended specifically for comparing foundation models using a consistent prompt set and producing structured results with minimal custom tooling. In a Bedrock evaluation workflow, you provide an input dataset of prompts, typically in JSON Lines format so each line represents one evaluation record. Storing the JSONL file in Amazon S3 allows Bedrock to read the dataset at scale and write standardized evaluation outputs back to S3 for downstream analysis, sharing, and retention. The key requirement is to assess both quality and safety across multiple models. A Bedrock evaluation job can use a judge model to score the generated outputs against defined criteria. This approach supports repeatable, apples-to-apples comparisons because the same judge model and scoring rubric can be applied to every candidate foundation model. The candidate models are configured as generators, meaning each evaluation job run uses one selected FM to produce answers for the same prompt set, and the judge model evaluates those answers. That matches the requirement to generate evaluation reports that help a data scientist select the best FM. Option A does not use Bedrock evaluation jobs, and a knowledge base plus RetrieveAndGenerate is a RAG pattern, not an evaluation framework. It would produce responses but not standardized scoring and reporting suitable for model selection. Option C is incorrect because Bedrock evaluation outputs are delivered to S3, not directly to a BI destination, and selecting the candidate FM as the evaluator conflicts with the intended pattern of using a stable judge model. Option D misuses knowledge bases and retrieval evaluation types when the requirement is prompt-based model assessment rather than evaluating retrieval quality."
    },
    "category": "Testing, Validation, and Troubleshooting",
