    "explanation": {
      "zh": "选项 B 是正确的解决方案，因为它直接利用了亚马逊 Bedrock 的原生性能优化功能来解决吞吐量瓶颈和延迟要求，这些功能专为实时、高容量的生成式人工智能工作负载而设计。亚马逊 Bedrock 支持跨区域推理配置文件，这使得应用程序能够透明地将推理请求路由到多个 AWS 区域。在使用高峰期，流量会自动分配到有可用容量的区域，从而减少限流、请求排队和超时的风险。这种方法符合 AWS 关于构建高可用、低延迟且能跨地理边界弹性扩展的生成式人工智能应用程序的指导原则。通过在适用的情况下将多个推理请求合并为单个模型调用，批处理进一步提高了效率。AWS 生成式 AI 文档强调批处理是一种关键的优化技术，可减少每次请求的开销，提高吞吐量，并更好地利用模型容量。这对于像 Claude 3 Haiku 这样旨在实现快速响应和高请求量的轻量级、低延迟模型尤其有效。选项 A 不符合要求，因为在单个区域购买预配置的吞吐量会形成区域瓶颈，并且无法解决多区域可用性或超出预留容量的流量峰值问题。重试会增加负载和延迟，而不是解决根本原因。选项 C 改善了应用层的扩展性，但并未解决模型端的吞吐量限制。客户端的轮询路由缺乏对实时模型容量的感知，仍有可能将流量发送到已饱和的区域。选项 D 不合适，因为具有异步检索功能的批量推理是为离线或非交互式工作负载设计的。它无法满足交互式 AI 助手严格的 2 秒响应时间要求。因此，选项 B 提供了最有效且符合 AWS 标准的解决方案，能够在高峰使用时段实现低延迟、全球可扩展性和高吞吐量。",
      "en": "Option B is the correct solution because it directly addresses both throughput bottlenecks and latency requirements using native Amazon Bedrock performance optimization features that are designed for real-time, high-volume generative AI workloads. Amazon Bedrock supports cross-Region inference profiles, which allow applications to transparently route inference requests across multiple AWS Regions. During peak usage periods, traffic is automatically distributed to Regions with available capacity, reducing throttling, request queuing, and timeout risks. This approach aligns with AWS guidance for building highly available, low-latency GenAI applications that must scale elastically across geographic boundaries. Token batching further improves efficiency by combining multiple inference requests into a single model invocation where applicable. AWS Generative AI documentation highlights batching as a key optimization technique to reduce per-request overhead, improve throughput, and better utilize model capacity. This is especially effective for lightweight, low-latency models such as Claude 3 Haiku, which are designed for fast responses and high request volumes. Option A does not meet the requirement because purchasing provisioned throughput in a single Region creates a regional bottleneck and does not address multi-Region availability or traffic spikes beyond reserved capacity. Retries increase load and latency rather than resolving the root cause. Option C improves application-layer scaling but does not solve model-side throughput limits. Client-side round-robin routing lacks awareness of real-time model capacity and can still send traffic to saturated Regions. Option D is unsuitable because batch inference with asynchronous retrieval is designed for offline or non- interactive workloads. It cannot meet a strict 2-second response time requirement for an interactive AI assistant. Therefore, Option B provides the most effective and AWS-aligned solution to achieve low latency, global scalability, and high throughput during peak usage periods."
    },
    "category": "Operational Efficiency and Optimization for GenAI Applications",
    "source": "AIP_C01 Exam Q&A(119)",
    "num": 31
