    "stem": {
      "zh": "一家酒店公司希望增强其基于 Java 的传统酒店管理系统（PMS），并为其添加人工智能功能。该公司希望利用亚马逊 Bedrock 知识库为员工提供房间可用性信息和酒店特定详情。该解决方案必须为公司管理的每家酒店分别设置访问控制。该解决方案必须近乎实时地提供房间可用性信息，并且在高峰使用时段保持稳定的性能。哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？",
      "en": "A hotel company wants to enhance a legacy Java-based property management system (PMS) by adding AI capabilities. The company wants to use Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases to provide staff with room availability information and hotel-specific details. The solution must maintain separate access controls for each hotel that the company manages. The solution must provide room availability information in near real time and must maintain consistent performance during peak usage periods. Which solution will meet these requirements?"
    },
    "options": {
      "zh": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "部署一个包含所有酒店综合数据的单个亚马逊 Bedrock 知识库。配置 AWS Lambda 函数，通过直接的 API 连接从每个酒店的 PMS 数据库同步数据。使用带有酒店特定筛选器的 AWS CloudTrail 日志记录来审核每个酒店数据的访问日志。"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "为每家酒店创建一个由 PMS 数据库变更触发的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置该规则，使其将更新发送到管理 AWS 账户中的集中式 Amazon Bedrock 知识库。配置基于资源的策略以实施特定于酒店的访问控制。"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "在多账户结构中为每家酒店实施一个亚马逊 Bedrock 知识库。使用直接数据摄取来提供近乎实时的房间可用性信息。为不太关键的信息安排定期同步。"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "构建一个使用多个知识库的集中式亚马逊 Bedrock 代理解决方案。使用 AWS IAM 身份中心并设置酒店特定的权限集来控制员工访问权限。"
        }
      ],
      "en": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "Deploy a single Amazon Bedrock knowledge base that contains combined data for all hotels. Configure AWS Lambda functions to synchronize data from each hotel’s PMS database through direct API connections. Implement AWS CloudTrail logging with hotel-specific filters to audit access logs for each hotel’s data."
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for each hotel that is invoked by changes to the PMS database. Configure the rule to send updates to a centralized Amazon Bedrock knowledge base in a management AWS account. Configure resource-based policies to enforce hotel-specific access controls."
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "Implement one Amazon Bedrock knowledge base for each hotel in a multi-account structure. Use direct data ingestion to provide near real-time room availability information. Schedule regular synchronization for less critical information."
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "Build a centralized Amazon Bedrock Agents solution that uses multiple knowledge bases. Implement AWS IAM Identity Center with hotel-specific permission sets to control staff access."
        }
      ]
    },
    "explanation": {
      "zh": "选项 C 最符合要求，因为它遵循了 AWS 在数据隔离、访问控制和可扩展的 GenAI 检索方面的最佳实践。为每家酒店单独设置一个 Amazon Bedrock 知识库，确保了数据和权限的严格分离。这种方法自然地实现了酒店级别的访问控制，无需复杂的策略逻辑或查询后的过滤。多账户结构通过将每个酒店的数据平面隔离开来进一步增强了安全性和治理能力。AWS 建议对具有严格租户或合规性边界的工作负载进行账户级别的隔离。酒店员工仅能访问其所在酒店的账户及相应的知识库，从而消除了跨酒店数据泄露的风险。直接将数据导入每个知识库，能够实现诸如房间可用性等关键数据的近乎实时更新。对于不经常变化的信息，通过计划同步可降低数据导入成本，同时保持准确性。这种混合式数据导入模式在数据新鲜度和运营效率之间实现了平衡。由于亚马逊 Bedrock 知识库是完全托管的，因此在高峰使用期间性能保持稳定，无需公司管理索引、扩展或检索基础设施。每个知识库都独立扩展，避免了集中式设计中可能出现的“吵闹邻居”问题。选项 A 和 B 依赖于集中式知识库，这会增加策略的复杂性，并带来访问控制配置错误的风险。选项 D 增加了不必要的编排复杂性，并且本身无法解决实时数据新鲜度的要求。因此，选项 C 为利用亚马逊 Bedrock 知识库增强 PMS 提供了最安全、可扩展且操作效率最高的解决方案。",
      "en": "Option C best meets the requirements by aligning with AWS best practices for data isolation, access control, and scalable GenAI retrieval. Implementing a separate Amazon Bedrock knowledge base for each hotel ensures strict separation of data and permissions. This approach naturally enforces hotel-level access control without requiring complex policy logic or post-query filtering. A multi-account structure further strengthens security and governance by isolating each hotel’s data plane. AWS recommends account-level isolation for workloads with strong tenancy or compliance boundaries. Hotel staff can be granted access only to their hotel’s account and corresponding knowledge base, eliminating the risk of cross-hotel data exposure. Direct data ingestion into each knowledge base enables near real-time updates for critical data such as room availability. For information that does not change frequently, scheduled synchronization reduces ingestion cost while maintaining accuracy. This hybrid ingestion model balances freshness and operational efficiency. Because Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases are fully managed, performance remains consistent during peak usage periods without the company managing indexing, scaling, or retrieval infrastructure. Each knowledge base scales independently, preventing noisy-neighbor issues that could arise in a centralized design. Option A and B rely on a centralized knowledge base, which increases policy complexity and introduces risk of misconfigured access controls. Option D adds unnecessary orchestration complexity and does not inherently solve real-time data freshness requirements. Therefore, Option C provides the most secure, scalable, and operationally efficient solution for enhancing the PMS with Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases."
    },
    "category": "Foundation Model Integration, Data Management, and Compliance",
    "source": "AIP_C01 Exam Q&A(119)",
    "num": 75
