    "explanation": {
      "zh": "选项 A 最能满足捕捉多跳、高度互联关系的需求，同时操作开销最小。传统的向量相似性搜索在查找语义相似的文本方面表现出色，但对于基于实体间关系的推理（尤其是当分析师需要间接的、多跳的连接，例如基金 # 持有 # 发行人 # 行业 # 法规）却未进行优化。基于图的检索正是为这类关系遍历而设计的。 GraphRAG 将检索增强生成与图感知上下文选择相结合。通过在图存储中表示实体及其关系，该系统能够遍历多个节点以汇集一套全面的相关事实。这提高了完整性，并降低了模型遗漏对准确投资指导至关重要的间接关系的可能性。亚马逊 Neptune Analytics 提供了一个托管的图分析环境，能够高效地遍历和分析复杂的关系网络。当与亚马逊 Bedrock 知识库集成时，它通过提供适用于生成式人工智能应用的托管式摄取、检索和编排模式，减少了定制工程的需求。与构建和维护自定义的多阶段检索逻辑相比，这降低了运营开销。使用经过图优化的引擎来满足低于 3 秒的要求也更为可行，因为多跳遍历能够高效执行，这比在应用层串联多个向量搜索并合并结果要高效得多。知识库和 Neptune Analytics 的托管特性降低了维护、扩展和运营负担，同时还能实现强劲的性能。选项 B 和 C 需要大量的自定义逻辑和编排，从而增加了复杂性和延迟。选项 D 并非为图形式的多跳探索而设计，需要大量的自定义索引和检索逻辑。因此，选项 A 是在多跳关系感知 RAG 中与 AWS 最为契合且操作效率最高的方案，具有出色的性能。",
      "en": "Option A best satisfies the requirement to capture multi-hop, highly interconnected relationships with minimal operational overhead. Traditional vector similarity search excels at finding semantically similar text but is not optimized for reasoning over explicit entity-to-entity relationships, especially when analysts need indirect, multi-hop connections (for example, fund # holding # issuer # sector # regulation). Graph-based retrieval is designed specifically for these kinds of relationship traversals. GraphRAG combines retrieval-augmented generation with graph-aware context selection. By representing entities and their relationships in a graph store, the system can traverse multiple hops to assemble a holistic set of relevant facts. This improves completeness and reduces the chance that the model misses indirect relationships that are essential for accurate investment guidance. Amazon Neptune Analytics provides a managed graph analytics environment capable of efficiently traversing and analyzing complex relationship networks. When integrated with Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases, it reduces custom engineering by providing managed ingestion, retrieval, and orchestration patterns suitable for GenAI applications. This lowers operational overhead compared to building and maintaining custom multi- stage retrieval logic. Meeting the sub-3-second requirement is also more feasible with a graph-optimized engine because multi-hop traversals can be executed efficiently compared to chaining multiple vector searches and joining results in an application layer. The managed nature of Knowledge Bases and Neptune Analytics reduces maintenance, scaling, and operational burden while enabling strong performance. Option B and C require extensive custom logic and orchestration, increasing complexity and latency. Option D is not designed for graph-style multi-hop exploration and would require significant custom indexing and retrieval logic. Therefore, Option A is the most AWS-aligned and operationally efficient approach for multi-hop relationship- aware RAG with strong performance."
    },
    "category": "Foundation Model Integration, Data Management, and Compliance",
    "source": "AIP_C01 Exam Q&A(119)",
