    "explanation": {
      "zh": "正确答案是 B 和 C，因为它们直接解决了幻觉减少的问题，同时保持了高吞吐量和低延迟。选项 B 通过检索增强生成（RAG）将模型输出与经过验证的内容相结合，从源头上减少幻觉。使用带有语义分块功能的亚马逊 Bedrock 知识库，确保将长篇技术文档分解为有意义且连贯的片段。这使得模型只需检索最相关的片段，而无需一次性处理整个文档，从而显著提高事实准确性并减轻模型的认知负担。这种方法可高效扩展，每小时能够处理超过 1000 份文档。选项 C 通过使用亚马逊 Bedrock 安全防护措施来检测和阻止类似幻觉的输出模式，从而增加了一层纵深防御的安全层。防护措施在推理时运行，对性能的影响极小，因此适合低延迟要求。虽然防护措施不能完全消除幻觉，但能有效防止不安全或明显捏造的输出到达用户。选项 A 由于明确的推理步骤而增加了延迟和成本，并且对于高吞吐量的工作负载扩展性不佳。选项 D 增加了随机性并使幻觉情况恶化。选项 E 重复了现有的错误方法。因此，选项 B 和选项 C 共同提供了可扩展的接地和运行时保护，满足了准确性、性能和吞吐量的要求。",
      "en": "The correct answers are B and C because they directly address hallucination reduction while maintaining high throughput and low latency. Option B reduces hallucinations at their source by grounding model outputs in verified content through Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG). Using an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base with semantic chunking ensures that long technical documents are broken into meaningfully coherent sections. This allows the model to retrieve only the most relevant chunks, rather than processing an entire document in one pass, which significantly improves factual accuracy and reduces cognitive overload on the model. This approach scales efficiently and supports processing more than 1,000 documents per hour. Option C adds a defense-in-depth safety layer by using Amazon Bedrock guardrails to detect and block hallucination-like output patterns. Guardrails operate at inference time with minimal performance overhead, making them suitable for low-latency requirements. While guardrails do not eliminate hallucinations entirely, they effectively prevent unsafe or clearly fabricated outputs from reaching users. Option A increases latency and cost due to explicit reasoning steps and does not scale well for high- throughput workloads. Option D increases randomness and worsens hallucinations. Option E repeats the existing flawed approach. Therefore, Options B and C together provide scalable grounding and runtime protection that meet accuracy, performance, and throughput requirements."
    },
    "category": "Testing, Validation, and Troubleshooting",
    "source": "AIP_C01 Exam Q&A(119)",
    "num": 85
