    "explanation": {
      "zh": "此要求明确需要逐字符流式传输、长时间运行的响应、低延迟和大规模并发，这与亚马逊 Bedrock 流式推理模式完全一致。亚马逊 Bedrock 提供了 InvokeModelWithResponseStream API，专门用于在生成标记时流式传输模型的部分输出。这使得用户能够近乎即时地获得反馈，而无需等待完整响应的完成，这对于响应时间长达 45 秒的情况至关重要。亚马逊 API 网关的 WebSocket API 专为双向、低延迟、服务器主动发起的通信而设计，允许后端实时向客户端推送字符或令牌。这消除了低效的轮询，并支持数千个并发的开放连接。 AWS Lambda 与 WebSocket API 原生集成，并能根据连接量自动扩展，从而实现完全托管的无服务器架构。这种方法在避免客户端直接访问 Bedrock API 的同时，还能保持安全性、集中式身份验证、节流和可观测性。选项 B 会引入轮询延迟和不必要的 API 开销，并且无法提供真正的流式传输。选项 C 违反了 AWS 的安全最佳实践，直接将 Bedrock 暴露给客户端，并且无法安全地扩展。选项 D 只能提供已完成的响应，无法满足实时流式传输的要求。因此，选项 A 是唯一一个完全满足流处理行为、并发性、延迟和托管服务限制的解决方案。",
      "en": "This requirement explicitly calls for character-by-character streaming, long-running responses, low latency, and massive concurrency, which aligns directly with Amazon Bedrock streaming inference patterns. Amazon Bedrock provides the InvokeModelWithResponseStream API specifically for streaming partial model outputs as tokens are generated. This enables near-instant feedback to users instead of waiting for the full response to complete, which is essential when responses last up to 45 seconds. Amazon API Gateway WebSocket APIs are purpose-built for bidirectional, low-latency, server-initiated communication, allowing the backend to push characters or tokens to clients in real time. This eliminates inefficient polling and supports thousands of concurrent open connections. AWS Lambda integrates natively with WebSocket APIs and scales automatically with connection volume, enabling a fully managed, serverless architecture. This approach maintains security, centralized authentication, throttling, and observability while avoiding direct client access to Bedrock APIs. Option B introduces polling latency and unnecessary API overhead and does not provide true streaming. Option C violates AWS security best practices by exposing Bedrock directly to clients and does not scale securely. Option D only serves completed responses and cannot meet the real-time streaming requirement. Therefore, Option A is the only solution that fully satisfies streaming behavior, concurrency, latency, and managed-service constraints."
    },
    "category": "Implementation and Integration",
    "source": "AIP_C01 Exam Q&A(119)",
    "num": 95
